From 23ff47eab6f682f08fe0dac38546a877652112f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 19:43:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] video: rockchip: mpp: forward-port MPP core and
 rkvdec2/rkvenc2 to 6.18

Forward-port the RK3588 vendor MPP service core and the rkvdec2/rkvenc2
codec drivers onto the mainline 6.18 IOMMU/DMA APIs and the Rockchip/VSI
provider hooks. Drop the compat <soc/rockchip/rockchip_iommu.h> shim (now
provided in-tree) and delete it.

Notable changes:
  - use the Rockchip provider fault/refresh/mask hooks instead of
    BSP-private IOMMU APIs;
  - rkvdec2 CCU attach now establishes an explicit cluster shared IOMMU
    domain via mpp_iommu_shared_domain_*(): core 0 owns the shared domain
    and secondary cores join it (borrowing its rw_sem too), replacing the
    open-coded per-core domain field swap and bringing the decoder up to the
    encoder's serialization level;
  - EPROBE_DEFER-safe CCU/core probe ordering with proper unwind;
  - 6.18 dma-buf (_unlocked map/unmap) and iommu_map() gfp updates;
  - rk-mpp uapi: add MPP_CMD_SET_ERR_REF_HACK and the REG_OFFSET_ALONE /
    POLL_NON_BLOCK flags (REG_NO_OFFSET kept as an alias).

The rkvenc2 CCU attach still uses the older in-place field swap; converting
it onto mpp_iommu_shared_domain_*() is a follow-up. No userspace ABI change
(/dev/mpp_service preserved). Add the mpp-service, rkvdec2 and rkvenc2
devicetree bindings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
